{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>ra' ayin</b> — [meaning] an evil eye. And <i>ra'at ayinekha</i> ('your eye shall be evil') is construct state, lacking [the word] <i>'ish</i>. Likewise <i>tov ayin</i> ['good of eye'] — it is <i>yiborakh</i> (he will be blessed), and the proper reading is <i>'ish tov ayin</i>. [n: The Hebrew forms cited (רעה עינך, יבורך, איש טוב עין) reference Deut. 15:9 and Prov. 22:9; translated literally where Ibn Ezra quotes them as grammatical examples.]"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:19.309343902Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}